 "note": "Entity shape-descriptor table (6de3:b91a, 96 x 28-byte records), indexed by entity type (the same value stored in level-script records -- see docs/formats/pin-level-script.md). frameSourceMode (descriptor+0x16, copied to global [0x89e4] in Gfx_DrawObject) is the addressing-mode switch confirmed via raw disassembly: nonzero (1) -> the entity's current animation frame (initialized to animStart) is used DIRECTLY as a flat tile index into bankAtlas[bankId]'s combined tile space (same mechanism already confirmed for bankId 6). 0 -> tile index is instead read (one byte, first of possibly `frameCount` for tall composite sprites) from a per-(kind,frame) byte-stream reached via a 3-way near-pointer table (6de3:e4fa/e906/dea2, selected by `kind`) indexed by [animStart*2] -- NOT YET extracted, still renders as a dot. 0xffff -> reads from live EGA/VGA video memory (a screen-grab special effect, e.g. a portal/mirror), not a bank tile -- always a dot. `kind` is descriptor+0x18, only meaningful for selecting the frameSourceMode=0 near-pointer table.",
